<title>USA: Shoe Carnival June same-store sales up.</title>
<headline>Shoe Carnival June same-store sales up.</headline>
<dateline>EVANSVILLE, Ind. 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shoe Carnival Inc said same-store sales for the five weeks ended July 5 rose 10.7 percent.</p>
<p>Total sales for the period rose 11.2 percent to $24.0 million from $21.6 million for the five weeks ended July 6, 1996.</p>
<p>Sales for the first five months of 1997 grew 4.2 percent to $103.0 million from $98.9 million for the first five months of 1996.  Same-store sales rose 5.2 percent for the 22-week period, said the footwear seller.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
